diagrams, and associated artifacts — collectively "the Software").

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. FREE NON-COMMERCIAL USE
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

You are granted a worldwide, royalty-free, perpetual, non-exclusive license to:

• Use, copy, modify, and distribute the Software for any **non-commercial** purpose,
  including research, education, personal projects, open-source development,
  benchmarking, and internal evaluation.

• Create derivative works and distribute them under the same terms.

"Non-commercial" means not for monetary compensation, not as part of a paid
service, not embedded in a product sold or licensed to third parties, and not
used to generate revenue directly or indirectly.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. COMMERCIAL USE — ROYALTY OBLIGATION
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Any **commercial use** of the Software requires payment of a **20% royalty** on
Net Commercial Revenue attributable to the Software.

2.1 Definition of Commercial Use
   Commercial use includes, but is not limited to:
   • Offering inference-as-a-service, APIs, or hosted solutions using the Software
   • Embedding the Software in proprietary products or services sold to customers
   • Using the Software to reduce infrastructure costs in a for-profit operation
   • Reselling compute capacity orchestrated by the Software
   • Any use where the Software contributes to revenue generation

2.2 Royalty Calculation
   • Royalty Rate: 20% (twenty percent)
   • Base: Net Commercial Revenue = Gross Revenue − Direct Costs
     – Direct Costs include: electricity, hardware depreciation, bandwidth,
       third-party cloud fees, payment processing fees
     – Direct Costs do NOT include: R&D, salaries, marketing, overhead
   • Attribution: Revenue is attributable to the Software if the Software
     performs any part of the inference pipeline, scheduling, settlement,
     or orchestration for the commercial workload

2.3 Payment Terms
   • Reports and payments due quarterly (within 30 days of quarter end)
   • Minimum annual royalty: $10,000 USD (creditable against actual royalties)
   • Payable in USD or equivalent cryptocurrency (NEXUS token at 30-day VWAP)
   • Late payments accrue interest at 1.5% per month

2.4 Audit Rights
   Licensor may audit Licensee's books annually with 30 days' notice to verify
   royalty calculations. If underpayment exceeds 5%, Licensee bears audit costs.

